"title": "Whale shark observation 1791287","date": "2012-02-27","creator": "Blogie Robillo","description": "I've had this whale shark entered into the whaleshark.org database and nicknamed him Bruno. He approached our boat during our dive day's surface interval around noon. By my estimate he measured around 5m long that time. This individual seemed very curious of us. While I was in the water with him, he looked like he was \"sniffing\" the underside of the boat, as if waiting for something. My guess is this guy's been to Oslob, Cebu, where they feed whale sharks for the enjoyment of tourists.","subject": "Whale shark (Rhincodon typus)", 
"id": "inaturalist-observations-1791287.html"

