"title": "Whale shark observation 10413020","date": "2018-03-19","creator": "Jay Clue","description": "Seen at 30 meters underwater on the inner Gordo Banks. Circled us for a few moments early in the dive then came back about 30 minutes later at around 20 meters. Was one of the thickest whale sharks in terms of girth that I’ve ever encountered. Wondering if she is pregnant judging by the fullness and bulging of the lower abdomen. Specimen was about 8-10 meters long.","subject": "Whale shark (Rhincodon typus)", 
