"title": "Whale shark observation 69493059","date": "2021-02-13","creator": "donnamareetomkinson","description": "This is the young whale shark which washed up on Double Island Beach yesterday, tide has rolled it over during the night and it has additional injuries on it now from other fish/birds feeding on it overnight. From the markings, they are saying it is the same whale shark that was beaching itself on Jan 27th at Little Cove, off Noosa National Park. The carcass was still laying on the beach when we returned home late this afternoon. Lots of people at the beach taking photo's of it.","subject": "Whale shark (Rhincodon typus)", 
