"title": "Whale shark observation 91611093","date": "2018-04-07","creator": "Bert Klangpremchitt","description": "Young and playful Juvenile Whale Shark (Rhincodon typus) with approximate length of 3.5 meters (11.4 ft) swimming along with remora around the tropical reef's filtering for plankton food at shallow water - near to surface on a sunny day. Remark: Vertical Plankton Filtering is rare - very uncommon behavior to be seen in Thailand. This juvenile has a severe injured mark on its back behind the prime dorsal fin. Happy day for scuba divers and snorkelers to have super close up experience with Whale Shark! Juvenile Whale Sharks can frequently be found at Chumphon National Marine Park, Thailand. Location: Southeast of Koh Ngam Now, Chumphon National Marine Park of Thailand. Date: April 07, 2018 Time: 12:03 Depth: 8 meters (26.2 ft) Water Temperature: 30°c","subject": "Whale shark (Rhincodon typus)", 
